#
# Keep the build context to what actually compiles. Everything else is either
# noise in the layer cache or, in the case of keys, something that must never
# be near an image build.

.git
.idea
*.pem
*.key
go.work
go.work.sum
docs
fixtures
scripts
CHANGELOG.md
README.md
# The README's demo chain, at the repository root only. Package testdata/
# directories are not matched by this pattern and stay in the context.
/testdata

# Binaries built at the repo root. The images build their own.
/proof
/proof-mcp

# LICENSE is deliberately NOT excluded: it is copied into the final images,
# because an image is a distribution and Apache-2.0 §4(a) asks that recipients
# get the licence text, not merely a label naming it.
#
# licenses/ is not excluded either: each image copies the THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES
# file for its binary, and the build stage checks the binary against it.
